{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":450855,"duration_api_ms":409937,"ttft_ms":4788,"ttft_stream_ms":2036,"time_to_request_ms":13,"num_turns":69,"result":"Implementation complete. Summary of the changes:\n\n**New package** `lib/promscrape/discovery/scaleway/`:\n- `scaleway.go` — `SDConfig` (project_id, zone, api_url, port, plus the standard `HTTPClientConfig`/`ProxyURL`/`ProxyClientConfig` for auth and proxy support like other providers) and label-building logic. Only `running` instances are discovered; labels include id, name, hostname, commercial type, architecture, status, zone, org/project ids, public/private IPv4, and tags.\n- `api.go` — HTTP client setup (`configMap` cache, per-config `MustStop`) and pagination against `/instance/v1/zones/{zone}/servers` using Scaleway's `total_count` field.\n- `scaleway_test.go` / `api_test.go` — unit tests with fake API responses (no network calls), covering label building, running/stopped filtering, public-vs-private IP fallback, response parsing, and multi-page pagination.\n\n**Wiring** into `lib/promscrape/config.go` and `lib/promscrape/scraper.go` — added `scaleway_sd_configs`, `ScalewaySDConfigs`, `MustStop` loop, `getScalewaySDScrapeWork`, and registered the periodic refresh via the new `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` flag (default 30s), following the exact pattern used for `digitalocean`/`hetzner`/`ovhcloud`.\n\n**Docs**: added a `scaleway_sd_configs` section to `docs/victoriametrics/sd_configs.md` (TOC entry + full config example, meta-labels, refresh interval) and a `tip` entry in `docs/victoriametrics/changelog/CHANGELOG.md`.\n\nSince Scaleway authenticates via a non-standard `X-Auth-Token` header rather than `Authorization: Bearer`, I didn't invent a custom auth field — users supply it through the existing generic `headers: [\"X-Auth-Token: <token>\"]` option already supported by every HTTP-based SD in this codebase, per the ticket's instruction to reuse existing conventions.\n\nVerified: `go build ./...` and `go vet ./lib/promscrape/...` are clean, all new and existing `lib/promscrape/...` tests pass, and I smoke-tested that a `scaleway_sd_configs` block parses correctly through the real YAML config loader (then removed that scratch test file). I did not touch the `*_common_flags.md` docs — those are regenerated by a separate release-time Makefile target that builds against a private enterprise checkout, not something hand-edited in normal PRs.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9dc993cd-9e9d-4724-8877-c9470a8ac7d3","total_cost_usd":3.336380100000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":120639,"cache_read_input_tokens":6732127,"output_tokens":39501,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":120639,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":131,"outputTokens":39501,"cacheReadInputTokens":6732127,"cacheCreationInputTokens":120639,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":3.336380100000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"9d855984-15aa-4c55-ba39-5e4a8279e1ef"}
